00:10:23,656 --> 00:10:24,756
All right, I've seen enough.

260
00:10:24,824 --> 00:10:25,857
Let's see what we're working with.

261
00:10:25,925 --> 00:10:27,626
Go ahead, throw a few at the old paws.

262
00:10:30,562 --> 00:10:32,263
What are you,
a North Korean seamstress?

263
00:10:32,331 --> 00:10:33,297
Not if that's bad.

264
00:10:33,365 --> 00:10:35,166
Get mad! Come on!

265
00:10:35,234 --> 00:10:37,169
If it helps, think of me
as somebody who annoys you.

266
00:10:39,038 --> 00:10:40,539
Ooh, that's it! That's... that's good.

267
00:10:40,607 --> 00:10:42,441
Britta, put your blouse back on.

268
00:10:42,509 --> 00:10:44,977
Oh! Ow!

269
00:10:45,045 --> 00:10:46,012
Boys, this is not a game.

270
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,147
You gotta be ready for anything.

271
00:10:47,215 --> 00:10:49,216
Dude, that is not cool!

272
00:10:49,283 --> 00:10:50,951
Well, that foxy Black girl thinks it is.

273
00:10:51,018 --> 00:10:52,786
Hmm? Ow!

274
00:10:52,854 --> 00:10:55,122
- What are you doing?
- Why does she have to be black?

275
00:10:55,190 --> 00:10:56,824
What is going on?

276
00:10:56,891 --> 00:11:03,830
We're trying to get Jeff
ready for the fiiiii...iiight.

277
00:11:03,898 --> 00:11:06,166
I couldn't think of another word.

278
00:11:06,234 --> 00:11:07,368
Idiot.

279
00:11:07,435 --> 00:11:10,370
He meant we were figh...

280
00:11:10,438 --> 00:11:12,005
...ting.

281
00:11:12,073 --> 00:11:13,474
It is hard to think of another word.

282
00:11:13,542 --> 00:11:15,075
You realize there's no
other way for me to take this

283
00:11:15,143 --> 00:11:16,210
than as a giant middle finger

284
00:11:16,277 --> 00:11:17,544
to the most important day of the year.

285
00:11:17,612 --> 00:11:19,046
December 10th?

286
00:11:19,114 --> 00:11:22,116
It's our Christmas,
and I'm having a party.

287
00:11:22,184 --> 00:11:24,551
Due to my divorce and my
relatives picking sides,

288
00:11:24,619 --> 00:11:25,986
this will be the only Christmas party

289
00:11:26,054 --> 00:11:27,587
I throw this year.

290
00:11:27,655 --> 00:11:30,991
Will you be there, or
will I have another family

291
00:11:31,058 --> 00:11:32,425
letting me down?

292
00:11:32,493 --> 00:11:36,663
I told him not to fight.
He wouldn't listen.

293
00:11:36,731 --> 00:11:40,133
I don't know what that is.

294
00:11:41,969 --> 00:11:43,902
Jeffrey,

295
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:46,171
I have two boys.

296
00:11:46,239 --> 00:11:48,006
And when we have a serious discussion,

297
00:11:48,074 --> 00:11:50,308
I find that a brownie
helps them to relax.

298
00:11:51,810 --> 00:11:54,845
So why do you hate me and Jesus?

299
00:11:54,913 --> 00:11:57,248
I don't think my brownie's working.

300
00:11:57,315 --> 00:11:59,050
Please don't do something so ugly

301
00:11:59,117 --> 00:12:00,751
on a day so important to me.

302
00:12:00,819 --> 00:12:02,720
Again, it's December 10th.

303
00:12:02,787 --> 00:12:05,223
You think religion is stupid?

304
00:12:05,290 --> 00:12:06,323
No, no.

305
00:12:06,391 --> 00:12:08,592
To me, religion is like Paul Rudd.

306
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:11,329
I see the appeal, and I would
never take it away from anyone.

307
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:13,097
But I would also never
stand in line for it.

308
00:12:13,165 --> 00:12:14,899
And look, Shirley,

309
00:12:14,967 --> 00:12:16,701
the die has been cast
with this crazy bully guy.

310
00:12:16,769 --> 00:12:19,271
He picked on Abed,
and he corrected my Spanish.

311
00:12:19,338 --> 00:12:22,208
So you go to your party,
and I'll see you soon.

312
00:12:22,275 --> 00:12:25,378
Jeffrey, I forbid you from fighting.

313
00:12:25,446 --> 00:12:28,715
Well, you don't get to.
You're not my mom.

314
00:12:28,782 --> 00:12:29,950
You're right.

315
00:12:30,017 --> 00:12:31,652
But if you show up for the fight,

316
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,454
don't show up for my party.

317
00:12:33,521 --> 00:12:34,655
Oh, come on, Shirley, don't be mad.

318
00:12:34,723 --> 00:12:36,823
I'm not mad. I'm disappointed.

319
00:12:36,891 --> 00:12:39,660
That's "mom" for mad.

320
00:12:45,758 --> 00:12:49,294
Oh, hash browns and applesauce...
That's nice.

321
00:12:49,362 --> 00:12:51,796
Oh, what is that interesting smell?

322
00:12:51,864 --> 00:12:54,099
It's a traditional Muslim dish.

323
00:12:54,166 --> 00:12:55,900
It looks delicious.

324
00:12:55,968 --> 00:12:58,269
I'm guessing as a woman
I won't be allowed to eat that.

325
00:12:58,337 --> 00:13:01,339
That's too bad.

326
00:13:01,407 --> 00:13:03,608
Oh, look, Britta brought
what she believes in...

327
00:13:03,676 --> 00:13:05,210
nothing.

328
00:13:05,277 --> 00:13:07,112
Where should I put my
Buddha incense holder?

329
00:13:07,179 --> 00:13:10,315
I'm pretty sure that's a bong.

330
00:13:10,383 --> 00:13:11,416
Where's Jeff?

331
00:13:13,619 --> 00:13:16,287
I guess he made his choice.

332
00:13:16,355 --> 00:13:18,123
I want to go to Jeff's fight.

333
00:13:18,190 --> 00:13:19,785
As I told Jeff,
no one that goes to the fight

334
00:13:19,852 --> 00:13:20,953
can come to my party.

335
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:21,954
He's dead to me.

336
00:13:22,021 --> 00:13:23,388
And if any of you leave,

337
00:13:23,456 --> 00:13:25,791
you'll be dead to me too.

338
00:13:25,858 --> 00:13:27,326
Let's sing.

339
00:13:27,393 --> 00:13:33,192
# Jesus is a friend of mine #

340
00:13:33,227 --> 00:13:33,398
everybody!

341
00:13:33,466 --> 00:13:35,467
# Jesus is a friend of mine #

342
00:13:35,535 --> 00:13:37,836
Come on, everybody.
You don't know it?

343
00:13:37,904 --> 00:13:40,005
You're banning Jeff from the party?

344
00:13:40,073 --> 00:13:41,406
That doesn't seem very Christian.

345
00:13:41,474 --> 00:13:44,409
Well, that's an
interesting point of view

346
00:13:44,477 --> 00:13:46,311
coming from an atheist.

347
00:13:46,379 --> 00:13:50,048
I did my best to create
a special Christmas

348
00:13:50,116 --> 00:13:52,784
for my one intact family, and...

349
00:13:52,852 --> 00:13:55,754
this is the thanks I get.

350
00:13:55,822 --> 00:13:58,890
Shirley, you are a guilt machine.

351
00:13:58,958 --> 00:14:00,359
And Annie knows a thing
or two about guilt.

352
00:14:00,426 --> 00:14:01,626
Am I right, Jew?

353
00:14:01,694 --> 00:14:03,662
Say the whole word!

354
00:14:03,730 --> 00:14:06,431
Jewie?

355
00:14:06,499 --> 00:14:08,367
You would never catch
a Jehovah's witness

356
00:14:08,434 --> 00:14:09,668
saying "Jewie".

357
00:14:09,736 --> 00:14:11,670
Tell it to the birthday
cake you never got.

358
00:14:11,738 --> 00:14:13,505
You know, there's an old Buddhist saying

359
00:14:13,573 --> 00:14:14,740
in my vision group.

360
00:14:14,807 --> 00:14:16,508
You are not a Buddhist.
You are in a cult.

361
00:14:16,576 --> 00:14:19,454
Suck it, Nietzsche!

362
00:14:19,522 --> 00:14:21,790
Guys, everyone's faith is weird.

363
00:14:21,857 --> 00:14:23,024
Let's just not talk about it.

364
00:14:23,092 --> 00:14:24,526
There's nothing weird
about Christianity.

365
00:14:30,066 --> 00:14:32,667
Guys! Guys! Guys! Guys!

366
00:14:32,735 --> 00:14:35,971
Are we really gonna let
religion divide us like this?

367
00:14:36,038 --> 00:14:38,139
I think there's one
thing we can all agree on.

368
00:14:38,207 --> 00:14:40,308
- I get 72 virgins in heaven.
- No.

369
00:14:40,376 --> 00:14:43,478
That we would all like to
have Jeff at this party.

370
00:14:43,546 --> 00:14:45,180
- Mm-mm.
- He can't come.

371
00:14:45,247 --> 00:14:46,948
- Shirley.
- Mm-mm.

372
00:14:47,016 --> 00:14:48,049
Shirley, listen.

373
00:14:48,117 --> 00:14:49,384
I get that this is your first Christmas

374
00:14:49,452 --> 00:14:51,720
since your husband left you,
and I don't know,

375
00:14:51,787 --> 00:14:53,989
maybe that's why you're
being so stubborn,

376
00:14:54,056 --> 00:14:56,558
because you're trying so
hard to re-create something

377
00:14:56,625 --> 00:14:59,227
